From: SoundTap <noreply@soundtap.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] wlcore: log a refused RX block-ack session at debug level

The wl18xx firmware refuses an RX block-ack session whenever it has no free
slot, and access points retry ADDBA for as long as the link is up. Each
refusal printed a warning: 1158 lines in four days on a Wireless Link, which
pushed everything else out of the kernel log. The refusal is handled (the
session is simply not set up), so it is debug information.
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/acx.c	2026-09-29 14:32:08.312096107 +0200
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ti/wlcore/acx.c	2026-09-29 14:32:08.316096085 +0200
@@ -1434,7 +1434,7 @@
 
 	/* sometimes we can't start the session */
 	if (ret == CMD_STATUS_NO_RX_BA_SESSION) {
-		wl1271_warning("no fw rx ba on tid %d", tid_index);
+		wl1271_debug(DEBUG_ACX, "no fw rx ba on tid %d", tid_index);
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 		goto out;
 	}
